Komorebi includes third-party software, linked into komorebi.exe from
crates.io, each under its own license:

- Slint (https://slint.dev), used under its GPL-3.0 option (it is dual
  licensed; GPL-3.0-only is compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later as a whole
  work under GPL-3.0). Its attribution is still shown in Settings > About.
- SQLite (https://sqlite.org), in the public domain, through rusqlite's
  bundled build (MIT).
- Other crates under permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause,
  BSD-3-Clause, BSL-1.0, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CC0-1.0, 0BSD, Unlicense) or
  MPL-2.0 (used unmodified; its source is on crates.io). deny.toml lists
  the licenses allowed. To list every crate in the Windows build with its
  license:

      cargo deny --locked list --layout crate

The icon (assets/komorebi.ico) was made for Komorebi and is under the
same license as the code (GPL-3.0-or-later).

No fonts or other third-party assets are bundled in the repository; the
interface uses the fonts installed with Windows.
